{'symbol': 'F', 'date': '2020-04-28 18:30:00', 'title': 'FORD MOTOR REPORTS Q1 LOSS OF $0.50 PER SHARE', 'text': "QUARTERLY LOSS PER SHARE 50 CENTS.QUARTERLY ADJUSTED LOSS PER SHARE 23 CENTS.QUARTERLY REVENUE $34.32 BILLION VERSUS $40.34 BILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $-0.12, REVENUE VIEW $32.34 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.EXPECTS SECOND-QUARTER ADJUSTED EBIT TO BE A LOSS OF MORE THAN $5 BILLION.QUARTERLY AUTOMOTIVE REVENUE $31.34 BILLION VERSUS $37.24 BILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.FIRST-QUARTER ADJUSTED FREE CASH FLOW WAS NEGATIVE $2.2 BILLION.SAYS RECORDED VOLUME-DRIVEN AUTOMOTIVE EBIT LOSS OF $177 MILLION IN QUARTER.SAYS STRONG FORD CREDIT PORTFOLIO PERFORMANCE IN QUARTER WAS OFFSET BY ABOUT $600 MILLION FROM INCREASED CREDIT-LOSS RESERVES, SOME HIGHER DEPRECIATION.SAYS BELIEVE THE COMPANY'S CASH IS SUFFICIENT TO TAKE CO THROUGH THE END OF THE YEAR.SAYS AT THE END OF FIRST QUARTER, FORD AND FORD CREDIT HAD $35.1 BILLION AND $28.0 BILLION IN LIQUIDITY, RESPECTIVELY.SAYS FORD CREDIT DELIVERED $30 MILLION IN Q1 EARNINGS BEFORE TAXES, DOWN $771 MILLION.SAYS BELIEVE COMPANY'S CASH IS SUFFICIENT TO TAKE CO THROUGH END OF THE YEAR, EVEN WITH NO ADDITIONAL VEHICLE WHOLESALES OR FINANCING ACTIONS.SAYS WHILE FORD SHUT DOWN PLANTS IN MARCH, CASH USE HAS REMAINED HIGH BECAUSE PRODUCTION SUPPLIER PAYABLES ARE ABOUT 45 DAYS.SAYS CASH OUTFLOW WILL BE SUBSTANTIALLY LOWER AFTER EARLY MAY AS FORD PAYS DOWN PRODUCTION SUPPLIER PAYABLES.SAYS EXPECTS Q2 ADJUSTED EBIT TO BE A LOSS OF MORE THAN $5 BILLION, AS YEAR-OVER-YEAR INDUSTRY VOLUMES DECLINE SIGNIFICANTLY IN EVERY REGION."}
